      "slug": "risc-box",
      "name": "RISC Box",
      "description": "A real machine on the enclave's CPU. RISC Box boots a full RISC-V Linux inside the attested enclave from OS images in your own S3 bucket and bridges its serial console to your browser, keystrokes in, SSE out, disk saves back to the bucket. The guest, its images, and any credentials you type exist only in enclave RAM; the operator sees S3 traffic, never your machine.",
